.TH MGIT 1 "2026-10-02" "Knowledge Islands" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&
.PP
mgit \- run commands across multiple Git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
\&
.SS General
\&
.TP
.B mgit
List the primary checkouts in the current set.
.sp
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIcommand\fR ...]
Run
.B git
with the supplied command and arguments in every selected checkout.
.TP
.B mgit [\fIoptions\fR] \-B \fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]
Run a command directly, without prefixing it with
.BR git ,
in every repository in the current set.
.SS Workspace management
\&
.TP
.B mgit register
Generate
.I .mgit.toml
manifests for the current tree.
.sp
.TP
.B mgit repair
Clone missing repositories declared by direct members in the current
.I .mgit.toml
manifest.
.SS Repository management
\&
.TP
.B mgit sync
Update clean tracking branches in the current set and summarize repositories
that changed or need attention.
.TP
.B mgit structure <standard|nested> [--dry-run]
Convert every eligible repository in the current set between standard and
nested structures.
.TP
.B mgit worktree \fIlist|status\fR
List worktrees or show their branch and cleanliness.
.TP
.B mgit worktree add \fIBRANCH\fR
Add a linked checkout for an existing remote branch in every structured
repository.
.TP
.B mgit worktree remove <path> [--force]
Remove one linked worktree.
.SS Shell integration
\&
.TP
.B mgit completion <shell>
Print shell completion source.
.TP
.B mgit help [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]]
Print contextual help for an mgit command.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&
.B mgit
runs a Git command, or an arbitrary command with
.BR \-B ,
across a set of repositories.
Before each invocation it prints the repository path and command.
With no command it prints the repository paths that would be used.
.PP
The reserved command tree consists of
.BR register ,
.BR repair ,
.BR sync ,
.BR structure ,
.BR worktree ,
.BR completion ,
and
.BR help .
Their subcommands and arguments are validated by
.BR mgit .
Other commands are passed to Git unchanged, so
.B mgit status --short
means the same Git command in every selected repository.
.B mgit help \fICOMMAND\fR
and
.B mgit \fICOMMAND\fR --help
print help scoped to that command.
.PP
When the current directory contains a
.I .mgit.toml
manifest,
.B mgit
uses the workspace's direct members, recursively expanding each child workspace.
Existing schema-1 manifests still select their configured default group.
The manifest is only valid in a non-Git container directory.
.PP
A repository leaf may contain
.IR .mgit.toml .
That file declares only cross-repository symlink metadata; it does not select
repositories or make a workspace.
.PP
Without a workspace manifest,
.B mgit
walks the current tree for Git repositories, omitting repositories nested
inside another repository.
Discovery stops at repository roots and never follows symlinked repositories
or container directories by default.
The
.B \-I
option ignores workspace manifests and always uses discovery instead.
.PP
With
.BR \-a / \-\-agora
or
.BR \-\-estate ,
.B mgit
invokes
.B ki agora roots --null
once and uses the returned local repository roots as its exact set.
This optional mode does not read KI configuration itself and requires
.B ki
on
.BR PATH .
.SH INSTALLATION
\&
.PP
On macOS or Linux, install the published release with Homebrew:
.PP
.nf
brew install knowledgeislands/tap/mgit
.fi
.PP
On any system with Bash and Git, install the current release with:
.PP
.nf
curl -fsSL https://knowledgeislands.info/install/mgit | bash
.fi
.PP
Pass an exact release with:
.PP
.nf
curl -fsSL https://knowledgeislands.info/install/mgit | bash -s -- vX.Y.Z
.fi
.PP
The installer writes the executable to
.I ~/.local/bin
and the manual to
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1
by default. Set
.B MGIT_INSTALL_DIR
or
.B MGIT_MAN_INSTALL_DIR
to choose different locations. Set
.B MGIT_VERSION
as an exact-version environment alias. A positional version takes precedence;
with neither input, the installer discovers the latest release.
.SH OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BR \-P , " \-\-physical"
Do not follow symlinked container directories.
This is the default.
Symlinked repositories are never followed.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-L , " \-\-follow-symlinks"
Follow symlinked container directories while discovering repositories.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-B , " \-\-bare"
Run the supplied command directly rather than as a
.B git
subcommand.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-I , " \-\-ignore"
Ignore
.I .mgit.toml
workspace selection and discover repositories by walking the tree.
Repository-kind symlink metadata still expands the discovered set.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-a , " \-\-agora" " \fINAME\fR"
Select the local roots resolved by
.B ki
for the named Agora.
MGit uses the resolver's NUL-delimited output. Ordinary commands invoke
.B ki
only when this selector is present. This selector cannot be combined with
.BR \-P ,
.BR \-L ,
.BR \-I ,
and it is unavailable to MGit management commands except
.BR register .
.sp
.TP
.B \-\-estate
Select every local root in the registered KI estate. This is exactly equivalent
to
.BR "\-\-agora estate" .
It has the same selection restrictions as
.BR \-\-agora ,
but cannot be used with
.BR register ,
and the two selectors cannot be combined.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-f , " \-\-filter" " \fIGLOB\fR"
Limit the repository set to repositories whose path, relative to the current
directory, matches the shell glob
.IR GLOB .
A bare pattern also matches a repository's last path component, so
.B mgit \-f 'mcp\-*'
selects the mcp repositories wherever they sit in the tree.
The option is repeatable; a repository matching any pattern is kept.
Workspace selection occurs before filtering.
The filter narrows normal commands, the repository listing, and the
.B structure
and
.B worktree
set commands; it does not affect
.B register
or
.BR repair .
.sp
.TP
.BR \-W , " \-\-all-worktrees"
Include every active linked worktree as well as the primary checkout when
listing repositories or running ordinary commands and
.BR sync .
Normal listings and command headers label worktrees outside the repository or
under its hidden Git storage as repository [branch], without the storage prefix.
Detached worktrees use their directory name and abbreviated commit.
Execution still uses the actual checkout path; use
.B worktree list
to inspect physical paths.
Without this option, a standard repository uses its root checkout and a nested
repository uses its required
.I main/
checkout. This option does not change
.B structure
or
.B worktree
management commands.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Print contextual help for the requested command and exit.
.sp
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Print the version and exit.
.SH COMMAND GROUPS
\&
.PP
mGit divides its commands into workspace management, repository management,
and shell integration. Run
.B mgit help
for the command list and
.B mgit help \fICOMMAND\fR
for exact command grammar.
.SS Workspace management
\&
.TP
.B mgit register
scans saved locations (default:
.BR local )
and writes a
.I .mgit.toml
in every non-Git container directory, listing child workspaces and repositories.
It writes a
.I .mgit.toml
only in a repository that owns cross-repository symlinks.
The command does not descend into repositories and refreshes direct members.
.B mgit register add
and
.B mgit register rm
change saved search locations and refresh generated entries in one invocation.
Both accept repeated and combined
.B \-\-agora
.I NAME
and
.B \-\-repo
.I PATH
options.
.B mgit register \-\-agora
.I NAME
is an add shorthand. Adding a repository path requires an existing Git
repository; removal accepts a saved relative path even after it disappears.
Later runs of
.B mgit register
refresh all saved locations, resolving Agora roots through
.BR ki .
Source resolution failure stops registration before writing. Ordinary commands
use generated repository entries without invoking
.BR ki .
The selected set combines local and additional members without duplicates.
.B mgit repair
uses only direct members and does not clone additional locations automatically.
.PP
When Chezmoi is installed and configured, generated manifests below its target
directory are added to Chezmoi's source state when possible. A Chezmoi failure
emits a warning but does not prevent a local manifest from being generated or
removed.
.TP
.B mgit repair
uses the workspace manifest in the current directory to clone every missing
repository among the direct members with a source URL.
It creates standard, nested, and bare repositories in their declared forms.
It recursively follows child workspaces through their direct members.
Existing paths are never replaced: a present repository must match its declared
structure, and child workspace directories and manifests must already exist.
.SS Repository management
\&
.TP
.B mgit sync
prints numbered progress for each selected checkout, then checks it with
.BR "git status --short" .
Worktrees with local changes print their status and are skipped. Clean tracking
branches run
.BR "git pull --ff-only" ,
then
.B git push
when local commits remain ahead of upstream.
The command announces pulls and pushes before they start.
With
.BR \-i " or " \-\-interactive ,
it asks before each pull and push; an empty answer skips the action.
If a pull is skipped, the checkout is not pushed.
Declined actions are counted at the end and do not cause failure.
If input ends before an answer, the command stops unsuccessfully.
.PP
Repositories that pulled or pushed commits are named. Already-current
repositories are collapsed into one final count. Bare repositories, detached
heads, branches without upstreams, divergence, and Git failures are reported
and make the command exit unsuccessfully without forcing a change.
.TP
.B mgit structure nested
converts each eligible clean, attached standard checkout to a nested repository.
.B mgit structure standard
performs the reverse conversion only when the nested repository has its required
.I main/
checkout and no other linked worktrees.
.PP
Both forms apply changes by default.
Pass
.B \-\-dry-run
to preview changes instead.
.TP
.B mgit worktree list
groups linked worktrees by their shared Git store.
.B mgit worktree status
shows each worktree's branch and cleanliness.
.PP
.B mgit worktree add \fIBRANCH\fR
adds a checkout for an existing
.B origin/\fIBRANCH\fR
to every structured repository after preflighting the full set. Nested
repositories receive
.I <repository>/<branch>
checkouts; standard repositories receive
.I <repository>/.git/mgit-worktrees/<branch>
checkouts.
.B mgit worktree remove <path>
removes one linked checkout and never removes the primary or required
.I main/
checkout.
Pass
.B \-\-force
to discard dirty changes in that linked checkout.
.SS Shell integration
\&
.TP
.B mgit completion bash
and
.B mgit completion zsh
print shell completion definitions to standard output.
They complete the command hierarchy and command-local flags.
.PP
For Bash, source the definition from the shell configuration:
.PP
.nf
source <(mgit completion bash)
.fi
.PP
For Zsh, write the definition to a file named
.I _mgit
in a directory on
.B fpath
before
.B compinit
runs. For example:
.PP
.nf
mkdir -p ~/.zsh/completions
mgit completion zsh > ~/.zsh/completions/_mgit
fpath=(~/.zsh/completions $fpath)
autoload -Uz compinit && compinit
.fi
.SH FILES
\&
.SS Workspace kind
\&
.PP
A
.I .mgit.toml
manifest uses an explicit workspace kind and path-keyed direct members.
The complete generated shape is:
.PP
.nf
kind = "workspace"
locations = ["local"]

[members."platform"]
kind = "repository"
type = "standard"
source = "git@github.com:acme/platform.git"

[members."workspace"]
kind = "repository"
type = "nested"

[members."archive.git"]
kind = "repository"
type = "bare"

[members."group"]
kind = "workspace"
.fi
.PP
Repository members require
.BR type ,
which is one of
.BR standard ,
.BR nested ,
or
.BR bare .
The optional
.B source
field is a clone URL. Workspace members use only
.BR kind .
Member paths are safe relative map keys below the manifest directory.
.PP
The
.B locations
array stores search source strings such as
.BR local ,
.BR agora:personal ,
and
.BR repo:../shared-tools .
When absent, it defaults to
.BR local .
Empty
.B [registered.members."PATH"]
tables hold generated repository roots as paths relative to the manifest
directory; these paths may reach outside the workspace. Older
.B agora
snapshots are migrated when registration runs.
.PP
Existing schema-1 manifests with grouped members remain readable.
Registration migrates one containing only the structural default group to
direct members. A manifest with alternative groups must have those tables
removed deliberately before registration; mgit refuses to discard them.
.SS Repository kind
\&
.PP
Repository-owned
.I .mgit.toml
files have a separate leaf-only purpose: their
.B symlinks
table maps a symlink the current repository owns to its target in another
repository:
.PP
.nf
kind = "repository"

[symlinks]
"link" = "target"
.fi
.PP
Blank lines and comments beginning with
.B #
are ignored.
.SH REPOSITORY STRUCTURES
\&
.PP
A standard repository is an ordinary checkout with a
.I .git/
directory. Worktrees added by
.B mgit
are placed below
.IR .git/mgit-worktrees/ .
A nested repository is an
.B mgit
controller containing a
.I .bare/
shared Git store, a
.I .git
controller file, and a required
.I main/
checkout.
Commands operate in live checkouts, never in the nested controller or bare
store.
.SH DEVELOPMENT INSTALLATIONS
\&
.PP
For development against this checkout, run
.B ./install.sh --link
to link the current executable and manual into
.B MGIT_INSTALL_DIR
(default
.IR ~/.local/bin )
and
.B MGIT_MAN_INSTALL_DIR
(default: the corresponding
.IR share/man/man1
directory). The linked command follows changes to this checkout and does not
download a release.
.PP
Link mode refuses to replace regular files. Use a dedicated development
directory or invoke
.B ./bin/mgit
directly when comparing it with a Homebrew or release installation. Use
.B man -l man/mgit.1
to inspect the checked-out manual regardless of the configured manual path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\&
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.sp
.TP
.B 1
An operation failed.
.sp
.TP
.B 2
The command grammar was invalid or an unsupported option was supplied.
.PP
For a fan-out command,
.B mgit
returns status 1 if any selected repository command fails, after attempting
every selected checkout. It returns 0 only when every command succeeds.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&
.BR git (1),
.BR git-worktree (1)
.PP
The project README and the guide collection are available at
.I https://github.com/knowledgeislands/tools-mgit .
.PP
The user guide lives under
.I docs/guides/user/
in that repository:
.I installation.md
covers installation and upgrades,
.I running-commands.md
covers command fan-out and selectors,
.I repository-sets.md
covers
.I .mgit.toml
manifests and registration, and
.I worktrees.md
covers the standard and nested repository structures.
